    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`get_w2_permute_indices_with_cache` stores its shuffle-index cache on the device by default. When memory saver releases the weights region, those device tensors are zeroed while the cache dict still holds them, so the next forward after resume computes garbage permutations. Keeping the permute indices on the host avoids the corruption; the indices are small and reused every forward.\n\nStandalone fix.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `python/sglang/srt/layers/quantization/mxfp4.py`: build the permute-index cache with `get_shuffle_matrix_a_idx_with_cache` / `get_shuffle_matrix_sf_a_idx_with_cache` on host tensors instead of the device-cached helper.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nMXFP4 MoE forward path unchanged; only the cache residency of the permute indices changes (host vs device).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo perf impact: the indices are already uploaded per use; keeping them on host removes a device allocation.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #34976077923](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34976077923)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #34976077190](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34976077190)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:start -->:x: [Run #34976077694](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34976077694)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n",
